\code{\link[=lag_ceiling]{lag_ceiling()}} and \code{\link[=lag_ceiling_boot]{lag_ceiling_boot()}}. A count series is more
concentrated than its own expectation, so the exceedance is inflated by
sampling variation in a way that no interval on it removes;
\code{\link[=lag_ceiling_stan]{lag_ceiling_stan()}} estimates the concentration of the expected series
instead, which is the object the bound actually applies to.
